We will talk about the types of of innate creative muscles that live within all of us, within you, yes, you.
我们将讨论我们所有人、你的内在创造力的类型，是的，就是你。

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:46.659
And we will talk about how these creative muscles evolve with us across life, work, art, and the pursuit of everything.
我们将讨论这些创造力如何在生活、工作、艺术和对一切事物的追求中与我们一起发展。

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:50.959
Today we're gonna chat about film and podcast media.
今天我们要讨论电影和播客媒体。

00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:59.079
My guest today is well-versed in both, he wears many hats, and our conversation takes us through the systems that support and interact with the artistry.
今天我的客人精通这两方面，他身兼数职，我们的谈话带我们了解了支持艺术并与艺术互动的系统。

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:07.069
Across the board, there's this kind of double consciousness in the way artistic, creative work finds its way into the world.
总的来说，艺术、创意作品进入世界的方式存在着这种双重意识。

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:17.550
On one side, there's the intensity of the creative work itself, the hours of writing, rehearsing, shooting, editing, stitching together details until they finally resolve into something coherent.
一方面，创意工作本身的强度，写作、排练、拍摄、编辑、缝合细节的时间，直到它们最终分解成连贯的东西。

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:27.270
On the other side, there is the preparation, the scaffolding of validation, the decks, the pitches, the budgets, the endless, like me, trust me, gestures.
另一方面，还有准备工作、验证的脚手架、平台、球场、预算，还有无尽的，像我一样，相信我，手势。

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:32.870
You'll hear Alec talk about that, that are required before many projects can even begin.
您会听到 Alec 谈论这一点，这是许多项目开始之前所必需的。

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:49.639
And by begin, I mean here, begin with the goal of being seen, being picked up, becoming the thing that launches someone into a place where the work can speak for itself and that someone can keep working in this stream so far as capitalism runs the game, okay?
我所说的开始，我的意思是，从被看到、被接受的目标开始，成为将某人带入一个工作可以自己说话的地方，并且只要资本主义运行游戏，某人就可以继续在这个流中工作，好吗？

00:02:49.639 --> 00:02:55.479
Hollywood, Hollywood, has built an empire on this double consciousness.
好莱坞，好莱坞，在这种双重意识上建立了一个帝国。

00:02:55.479 --> 00:03:07.879
It is a city where art and commerce are bound together so tightly that they appear inseparable where the beauty of a scene and the pressure of an opening weekend are measured on the same ledger.
在这座城市，艺术和商业紧密地结合在一起，似乎密不可分，场景的美丽和开幕周末的压力都在同一个账本上衡量。

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:20.000
To speak about Hollywood is to speak about an entire architecture of creativity, a system that provides opportunity and exposure, and also dictates form funding and legitimacy.
谈论好莱坞就是谈论整个创造力的架构，一个提供机会和曝光度、也决定形式资金和合法性的系统。

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.039
A film is not simply the work of its director and cast.
一部电影不仅仅是导演和演员的作品。

00:03:24.039 --> 00:03:33.080
It's also the work of financiers, distributors, marketing teams, and executives who determine and whether the work will even see the light of day.
这也是金融家、分销商、营销团队和高管的工作，他们决定这项工作是否会重见天日。

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.639
This structure is at once enabling and constraining.
这种结构既具有促进性又具有约束性。

00:03:35.639 --> 00:03:46.719
It allows something as vast and complex as a feature film to even exist, but it also requires the artist to frame their own imagination in ways that appeal to some gatekeepers.
它允许像故事片这样庞大而复杂的东西存在，但它也要求艺术家以吸引某些看门人的方式构建自己的想象力。

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:50.759
The Creative Act begins long before a camera rolls, right?
创意活动早在镜头开拍之前就开始了，对吗？

00:03:50.759 --> 00:04:00.699
It begins in the translation of vision into the pitch deck, into the log line, into a concise justification of why the work deserves to exist.
它首先将愿景转化为宣传材料、日志，以及为何该作品值得存在的简洁理由。

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:04.759
The podcast world has inherited many of the same dynamics.
播客世界继承了许多相同的动力。

00:04:04.759 --> 00:04:21.588
Just like Tarantino once used to be able to make reservoir dogs in a warehouse on a whisper in a dream, so too can I sit here in our tiny spare room that quadruples as bicycle storage in my desk in a dumping space for outdoor gear and toddler toys and put my thoughts in craft out there.
就像塔伦蒂诺曾经能够在梦中低声在仓库里制作水库狗一样，我也可以坐在我们小小的备用房间里，这个房间是我桌子上自行车存放处的四倍，还有一个用于户外装备和幼儿玩具的倾倒空间，把我的想法投入到手工制作中。

00:04:21.588 --> 00:04:25.399
Though I don't have Harvey Keitel, and thus it's just you and me.
虽然我没有哈维·凯特尔，所以只有你和我。

00:04:25.399 --> 00:04:38.399
What might have once seemed like a freer medium, just pressed record, let the conversation flow, upload it for anyone to hear, has quickly developed its own economies of scale, its own validation structures.
曾经看似更自由的媒介，只需按下录音，让对话流畅，上传给任何人听，现在已经迅速发展出自己的规模经济和自己的验证结构。

00:04:38.399 --> 00:04:48.399
A podcast needs a host, yes, but it also needs production schedules, advertising partnerships, distribution platforms, and metrics that prove value.
是的，播客需要主持人，但它也需要制作时间表、广告合作伙伴、分发平台和证明价值的指标。

00:04:48.399 --> 00:04:58.399
Behind every hour of conversation released into the world are countless invisible acts of coordination, emails, calendars, edits, sponsorship copies, social media prompts.
发布到世界上的每一个小时的对话背后都有无数无形的协调行为、电子邮件、日历、编辑、赞助副本、社交媒体提示。

00:04:58.399 --> 00:05:05.399
The work disappears into the final product and yet it is essential to the very possibility of the show.
该作品消失在最终产品中，但它对于展览的可能性至关重要。

00:05:05.399 --> 00:05:09.399
To be clear, I am all of the roles and we do not have a sponsorship department.
需要明确的是，我负责所有角色，而且我们没有赞助部门。

00:05:09.399 --> 00:05:15.709
There is a paradox of much of modern artistic creativity.
许多现代艺术创造力都存在悖论。

00:05:15.709 --> 00:05:20.709
The most ephemeral media often require the most relentless scaffolding.
最短暂的媒体通常需要最无情的脚手架。

00:05:20.709 --> 00:05:25.709
Episodes vanish into a stream, but the labor that sustains them is constant.
情节消失在溪流中，但维持它们的劳动却是持续不断的。

00:05:25.709 --> 00:05:31.709
Movies may be remembered for decades, but before they can exist, they must pass through this obstacle course.
电影可能会被人们记住几十年，但在它们存在之前，它们必须穿过这个障碍。

00:05:31.709 --> 00:05:39.709
In both cases for film and podcasting, the act of creation is inseparable from the structures that allow it to reach an audience.
对于电影和播客来说，创作行为都与其接触观众的结构密不可分。

00:05:39.709 --> 00:05:45.709
There's something instructive in noticing how creators move between these systems.
留意创作者如何在这些系统之间移动是有启发性的。

00:05:45.709 --> 00:05:52.949
Directing a film and producing a podcast may seem like entirely different crafts yet they share a common rhythm.
导演电影和制作播客似乎是完全不同的工艺，但它们有着共同的节奏。

00:05:52.949 --> 00:06:01.990
Establish the outline, the framework, set the stage, line up the ducks, and then let the unpredictable alchemy of collaboration bring something to life.
建立轮廓、框架、搭建舞台、排列鸭子，然后让不可预测的协作炼金术将一些东西变为现实。

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:06.430
A director can block a scene, but the actors will always bring their own nuance.
导演可以阻止一个场景，但演员总是会带来自己的细微差别。

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:14.230
A producer can schedule the recording, but the conversation will always unfold in ways that no outline can fully anticipate.
制作人可以安排录制时间，但对话总是会以任何大纲都无法完全预料到的方式展开。

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:22.160
Creativity, as we've heard on many of these episodes, so often thrives at the junction of order and play.
正如我们在许多这样的剧集中听到的那样，创造力往往在秩序和游戏的结合处蓬勃发展。

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.000
In today's conversation, we get into the way projects are set up.
在今天的谈话中，我们将讨论项目的设置方式。

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:33.720
Spreadsheets, fun spreadsheets, sequences of scenes ordered and reordered, and then the joy of stepping back to watch collaborators bring the unexpected.
电子表格、有趣的电子表格、排序和重新排序的场景序列，然后退后一步观看合作者带来意想不到的乐趣。

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:42.519
And what emerges is the broader truth about film, television, podcasting, creativity itself, that it oscillates between the structure and flow.
出现的是关于电影、电视、播客、创造力本身的更广泛的事实，即它在结构和流程之间振荡。

00:06:42.519 --> 00:06:48.199
Too much order, the work becomes lifeless, too much freedom, the work risks in coherence.
太多的秩序，工作就会变得毫无生气，太多的自由，工作就会面临连贯性的风险。

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:49.199
This is not a lament.
这不是哀叹。

00:06:49.199 --> 00:06:54.800
It is a recognition that modern creativity is always entangled with its systems of distribution and visibility.
人们认识到，现代创造力总是与其分配和可见性系统纠缠在一起。

00:06:54.800 --> 00:07:02.759
To make something is also to navigate the infrastructures that allow it to be seen, heard, or streamed, experienced.
制造某种东西还需要驾驭基础设施，使其能够被看到、听到、或流式传输、体验到。

00:07:02.759 --> 00:07:08.689
here today that my guest, Alec, reflects that this negotiation is not a distraction from his creativity.
